※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4647

※ A requirement constrains what a call gives a type parameter.  A function with
※ none takes the types its signature writes down, so there is nothing for one to
※ constrain: a pre-condition of it is a condition, an expression answering
※ `bool` -- about its parameters, or one the compiler answers, such as two types
※ compared.

fn f(a: u6) → u6 pre(⌜u6⌝ + ⌜u6⌝ → ⌜u6⌝):
    a

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    f(0u6)
